          "title": "CTB BPUP 3.1 (Week 3, Workout 1)",
          "url": "/c/4-week-butterfly-ctb-pull-up-programming/sections/579026/lessons/2182144",
          "description": "Remember to focus on making progress with every single rep! Even small improvements matter. Filming your sets can be a powerful way to track that progress over time. After reviewing your EMOM videos from today, how would you rate your ability to scoop through the CTB Butterfly complex? Are you lifting your feet and staying long through the movement, or are you driving to the bar with your knees? Knee drives may feel more efficient, but they often limit chest to bar contact by breaking the hollow position. An “immature scoop” doesn’t just affect your butterfly CTB, it can also hold you back in movements like kipping pull-ups and bar muscle-ups. Focus on refining the pattern, the payoff is worth it.",
